==== script 172
// Corrected at release 0.9.0 (step 9), before it shipped. A `glm` on six rows, one of them far
// out on the regressor (1e8) and well predicted, ended in an internal error: "the score of
// column 2 is not zero at the maximum". The likelihood is nearly flat in the direction of that
// row, so the fit stops when a further step would raise the log-likelihood by less than a part
// in 1e13, while the score along it, measured against the size of its terms, was still a few
// parts in a million. The self-check now measures the score by the gain one more step would
// bring (the Newton decrement), which is what convergence means. The formula fuzz target found
// it within minutes of being taught `glm`. The fit is given, the slope undetermined: its
// estimate is nothing beside its standard error.
let f = frame(u = [0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1], a = [0, 1e8, -2, -2, 0, -1])
let g = f.glm(u ~ a, family: binomial)
g
g.fit_measures().deviance
g.test(a == 0)
